# Milestone: M3
# Covers: TAG_STOP is not intercepted by a try/catch block; the catch clause
#         is skipped and TAG_STOP continues propagating outward.
#
# defer-to: T29
#
# Reason: requires UTag runtime (T29) and TAG_STOP absorption in the unwind
# walker.  The walker already has the correct logic at M3: UCLEANUP_TRY_FRAME
# only absorbs UEXEC_THROW (not TAG_STOP), so TAG_STOP propagates past catch
# clauses.  However, writing a meaningful urbiscript test requires tag.stop()
# to be callable, which needs UTag (T29).
#
# When T29 lands, implement this fixture by uncommenting the source below.
# Expected behaviour: catch block does not run; "skipped" is NOT printed.
# The stop propagates to the outer tag scope.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T29):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   var caught = 0;
#   t: { try { t.stop() } catch (e) { caught = 1 } };
#   caught
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 0
